        "raw": "<p>So, when you want to gain one of the benefits from invoking your collection (set a die face, cancel a minor twist, or establish story), you have to justify it with something that supposedly happened in that collection.&nbsp; But here&#39;s what I don&#39;t get:</p><ul><li>You have to &quot;include an editor&#39;s note.&quot;&nbsp; How?&nbsp; Is this just something the player says as part of their justification?</li><li>Apparently you have to not only name the collection but know the specific issue.&nbsp; How do you know what issues are part of the collection?&nbsp; The pregenerated Freedom Five don&#39;t say; only Sentinels megafans would know all the comics that might be part of those collections.&nbsp; (And even those don&#39;t totally make sense--Tachyon and AZ&#39;s first appearances were in Freedom Four Annual #1 and Freedom Five Annual #2, so they really ought to be part of the same collection, but aren&#39;t.)&nbsp; And for continuing characters, you erase the back issues from your character sheet to make the collection, so how do you remember what issues were in that collection?</li><li>Sure, the GM shouldn&#39;t require the players to have perfect recall about their previous game sessions, but it&#39;s likely that none of their previous games are applicable to the situation they want to use it in.&nbsp; They shouldn&#39;t be able to say, &quot;Oh, yeah, in the game we played last month, the villain was actually a Fleshchild all along, so now I know a little bit about how Biomancer operates,&quot; should they?&nbsp; Normally, as GM, I&#39;d totally veto that.</li></ul>",
