        "id": 210540,
        "name": "dprcooke",
        "username": "dprcooke",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dprcooke/{size}/1961_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-09T02:39:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>For this, I’d default to the GM tip on page 12 of the Guide…</p>\n<p>“Be flexible in adjudicating how players apply these bonuses. Don’t require perfect recall about what happened in a previous adventure. <b>The barest justification should work.</b> Remember, comics get retconned all the time.”</p>\n<p>As for the editors’ note, that’s one thing I’ll probably just ignore.  If the players are playing heroes in a comic (which is much more fun in my mind than being part of the writing staff) they’re not going to be saying “back in issue <span class=\"hashtag\">#12</span>”, they’ll be saying something like “the last time we fought a fleshchild”.</p>\n<p>Basically, just go with whatever is most fun for your players.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:40:54.631Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
