        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "For this, I'd default to the GM tip on page 12 of the Guide...\r\n\r\n\"Be flexible in adjudicating how players apply these bonuses. Don't require perfect recall about what happened in a previous adventure. <b>The barest justification should work.</b> Remember, comics get retconned all the time.\"\r\n\r\nAs for the editors' note, that's one thing I'll probably just ignore.  If the players are playing heroes in a comic (which is much more fun in my mind than being part of the writing staff) they're not going to be saying \"back in issue #12\", they'll be saying something like \"the last time we fought a fleshchild\".\r\n\r\nBasically, just go with whatever is most fun for your players.",
